r_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T21:54:00Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T21:54:00Z","body":"> > [@Visense6](https://github.com/Visense6) What techniques are you using for drawing? Is it mostly `draw_rect()` and `draw_circle()`?\n> \n> draw_rect() is a must, and requires a rectangle without color filling, by the way, I went to test version 3.6, and its draw_rect() can batch draw calls with or without color fill. But draw_circle () doesn't.Thank you for your help~\n\nYes, Godot 3.6 uses a different technique for batching and can batch items in several situations that the technique in 4.4 can't. \n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2932643162/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2933199796","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107042#issuecomment-2933199796","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107042","id":2933199796,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u1RO0","user":{"login":"Visense6","id":52338846,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzM4ODQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52338846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6","html_url":"https://github.com/Visense6","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Visense6/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T02:55:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T02:55:57Z","body":"> > > [@Visense6](https://github.com/Visense6) What techniques are you using for drawing? Is it mostly `draw_rect()` and `draw_circle()`?\n> > \n> > \n> > draw_rect() is a must, and requires a rectangle without color filling, by the way, I went to test version 3.6, and its draw_rect() can batch draw calls with or without color fill. But draw_circle () doesn't.Thank you for your help~\n> \n> Yes, Godot 3.6 uses a different technique for batching and can batch items in several situations that the technique in 4.4 can't.\n\nI don't particularly understand how the Godot source code works, but if I'm just making a 2D game, is it more stable to use version 3.6?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2933199796/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2941968809","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107042#issuecomment-2941968809","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107042","id":2941968809,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vWuGp","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T23:36:50Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T23:37:53Z","body":"I would just use a sprite that represents a circle instead of relying on `draw_circle()` if the circle's size doesn't change continuously. You can use [SVGTexture](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105375) for this in [4.5.dev5](https://godotengine.org/article/dev-snapshot-godot-4-5-dev-5/) to get automatic oversampling, which means it'll look crisp at any resolution.\n\nIn 4.4, you can also use GradientTexture2D with the radial fill mode and points configured to create a sharp edge, which will effectively create a circle texture procedurally.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2941968809/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3582815840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107042#issuecomment-3582815840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107042","id":3582815840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VjW5g","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T19:06:02Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T19:06:02Z","body":"Confirmed still present in v4.6.dev4\n\n>Godot v4.6.dev4 - Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (nvidia; 570.195.03) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 15.52 GiB memory","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3582815840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3612632976","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107042#issuecomment-3612632976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107042","id":3612632976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XVGeQ","user":{"login":"FeldrinH","id":5256211,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTYyMTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5256211?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH","html_url":"https://github.com/FeldrinH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeldrinH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T14:51:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T14:51:40Z","body":"I don't know if this is caused by this exact issue, but if you do `queue_redraw` every frame, then the performance of `draw_circle` is truly attrocious (at least on some hardware). On my laptop with Intel Xe integrated graphics, doing 2500 `draw_circle` calls with `queue_redraw` in `_process` pushes the FPS to around 10. For comparison `draw_rect` in the same configuration has stable 60 FPS.\n\nThe curious thing is that this extra time shows up under `_draw` in the profiler and the total rendering time in the visual profiler is around 1-2 ms, potentially indicating that the `draw_circle` function itself is slow, rather than the rendering.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3612632976/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644221605","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107042#issuecomment-3644221605","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107042","id":3644221605,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZNmil","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T23:29:18Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T23:29:18Z","body":"> On my laptop with Intel Xe integrated graphics, doing 2500 draw_circle calls with queue_redraw in _process pushes the FPS to around 10. For comparison draw_rect in the same configuration has stable 60 FPS.\n\n`draw_circle()` creates a lot more vertices ([hardcoded to 64 vertices per call](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1cf31805370716ce8160ddc1394b9820249a21f7/scene/main/canvas_item.cpp#L857-L858)) than `draw_rect()` (4 vertices per call). Unfilled circles are also slower to render than filled circles, since they rely on hardware line drawing which is rather inefficient (while filled line drawing only needs to draw a single polygon).\n\nRendering `2500 * 64 = 160,000` vertices isn't so bad for filled circles, but rendering 160,000 hardware lines for unfilled circles is asking a lot of the graphics driver (which results in the CPU being the bottleneck).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644221605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]